egation persisted through restrictive covenants, discriminatory lending, and land-use rules that shaped where housing could be built. A major ordinance revision took effect in 1957, amid urban renewal, highway construction, and suburban growth. After decades of piecemeal amendments, Chicago adopted a substantially rewritten zoning code in 2004. Later reforms supported denser development near transit and expanded mixed-use possibilities, while debates over affordability, displacement, and neighborhood control continued to define zoning politics.'''\nprint(len(p.split()))\nfor i,w in enumerate(p.split(),1): print(i,w)\nPY","timeout":null}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","usage":{"input":4798,"output":782,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":516,"totalTokens":5580,"cost":{"input":0.00047980000000000006,"output":0.00039099999999999996,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0008708}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790398782076,"responseId":"resp_00e81a80824e53fb016ab7513ee5a087d0a4328a1dd67ae5c8","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_iVMdR7hI6MYQ227ogh1rk5Q7|fc_00e81a80824e53fb016ab7514caf4c87d0865929e3cb7b5885","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"158\n1 Chicago’s\n2 zoning\n3 history\n4 reflects\n5 the\n6 city’s\n7 changing\n8 approach\n9 to\n10 growth,\n11 industry,\n12 and\n13 neighborhood\n14 life.\n15 The\n16 1909\n17 Plan\n18 of\n19 Chicago\n20 called\n21 for\n22 orderly\n23 expansion,\n24 parks,\n25 and\n26 grand\n27 boulevards,\n28 but\n29 did\n30 not\n31 itself\n32 create\n33 zoning\n34 law.\n35 Chicago\n36 adopted\n37 its\n38 first\n39 comprehensive\n40 zoning\n41 ordinance\n42 in\n43 1923,\n44 dividing\n45 land\n46 into\n47 residential,\n48 commercial,\n49 and\n50 industrial\n51 districts\n52 and\n53 regulating\n54 building\n55 height,\n56 bulk,\n57 and\n58 yards.\n59 This\n60 framework\n61 emerged\n62 during\n63 rapid\n64 industrialization,\n65 when\n66 residents\n67 and\n68 businesses\n69 sought\n70 to\n71 limit\n72 incompatible\n73 uses\n74 and\n75 control\n76 development.\n77 Although\n78 the\n79 Supreme\n80 Court\n81 had\n82 barred\n83 explicit\n84 racial\n85 zoning\n86 in\n87 1917,\n88 segregation\n89 persisted\n90 through\n91 restrictive\n92 covenants,\n93 discriminatory\n94 lending,\n95 and\n96 land-use\n97 rules\n98 that\n99 shaped\n100 where\n101 housing\n102 could\n103 be\n104 built.\n105 A\n106 major\n107 ordinance\n108 revision\n109 took\n110 effect\n111 in\n112 1957,\n113 amid\n114 urban\n115 renewal,\n116 highway\n117 construction,\n118 and\n119 suburban\n120 growth.\n121 After\n122 decades\n123 of\n124 piecemeal\n125 amendments,\n126 Chicago\n127 adopted\n128 a\n129 substantially\n130 rewritten\n131 zoning\n132 code\n133 in\n134 2004.\n135 Later\n136 reforms\n137 supported\n138 denser\n139 development\n140 near\n141 transit\n142 and\n143 expanded\n144 mixed-use\n145 possibilities,\n146 while\n147 debates\n148 over\n149 affordability,\n150 displacement,\n151 and\n152 neighborhood\n153 control\n154 continued\n155 to\n156 define\n157 zoning\n158 politics.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790398800873},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Trimming eight words**\n\n**Trimming eight words**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_00e81a80824e53fb016ab75151bdd887d0973163ede5e83fee\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqt1Fc_k-6UhJz0LTybtVreVRGiaH7AaUiGbZia6T__4GXEhgeB_ejvAKsFUoKHWrwbTj9pCMVAs6Yn2t1VJHaLLDmyiLVLR-bYb-zyJoT5Owry5qvFS-j75vCerTZqn_izqM85Ix_XGJ3dtavLeB-__NLTQ6W4a2jhb-vRa0GwDwgwYOWqyiyHc_qdGgi2AD_QcMLz4k13nKHw7or_f64jfNIfusXtA3BW6QP2s9HZrd3APknBjMwWygtQcWXD5jz4bTFCHLGL5_S6X7FpcwZIVerZlgO36JC7EDdy6BUwqZKWzi9bsrulDO0VEDlBY9FPxgL1YKlFczj62oDeBn8jPf87ra0J5lKR-v3YqbQvpgJQo0ZrPb8uTNMgzlqelm2hA6qBrW9-fPbbXTOyqBsSDDwJaKB2VW8x8y5CHQNbg9mNQO8BFlwmtAOLNCKuve3lvBrRR4aWKAta_V3fEy7TBRt3Q155PG0R7qRYOcB1L5dBZAu1JFpWpo-HDHN4p83ZisLdgFYZgxsP7yJv6SNR3jP1A2hN9WOQw